      "id": 73535,
      "name": "Envisioner",
      "username": "Envisioner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-09-15T00:05:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>One more way in which it'd be a lot easier to play virtual Sentinels than the physical game.&nbsp; Not only would it automate the math, but it would be possible (or rather practical) to timestamp every card in the exact sequence it was played, making it easy to resolve situations like this.</p><p>But, of course, to computerize the game, you'd have to nail down the exact rules in a bit more detail than &gt;G seems to prefer, given that they want to keep the core game simple enough that players can thumb-rule nearly every situation.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:53:15.623Z",
